# ☕ Java Data Types — Interview Notes

## 1. Types of Data Types

Java data types are divided into **2 categories**:

```text
Data Types
├── Primitive
└── Non-Primitive / Reference
```

### Primitive — 8 types

```text
byte
short
int
long
float
double
char
boolean
```

### Reference Types

Examples:

```text
String
Arrays
Classes
Interfaces
Objects
```

⚠️ `String` is **not** a primitive type.

---

## 2. Primitive Data Types

| Type      |          Size | Main Use              |
| --------- | ------------: | --------------------- |
| `byte`    |        1 byte | Small integers        |
| `short`   |       2 bytes | Small integers        |
| `int`     |       4 bytes | General integers      |
| `long`    |       8 bytes | Large integers        |
| `float`   |       4 bytes | Decimal values        |
| `double`  |       8 bytes | More precise decimals |
| `char`    |       2 bytes | Single character      |
| `boolean` | JVM-dependent | `true` / `false`      |

### Integer types

```java
byte a = 10;
short b = 100;
int c = 1000;
long d = 10000L;
```

### Floating-point types

```java
float x = 10.5f;
double y = 10.5;
```

`double` is the default type for decimal literals.

