# 7. `==` vs `.equals()`

### `==`

* Primitive → compares values
* Object → compares references

### `.equals()`

* Used for logical/content equality of objects, according to the class's `equals()` implementation.

Example:

```java
int a = 10;
int b = 10;

System.out.println(a == b);  // true
```

Object example:

```java
String s1 = new String("Hello");
String s2 = new String("Hello");

System.out.println(s1 == s2);       // false
System.out.println(s1.equals(s2));  // true
```

### Memory Trick

```text
==         → value / reference
.equals()  → logical/content equality
```

